cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Residual-level Hellings–Downs diagnostics for pulsar timing arrays: calibration failures and a pre-registered EPTA replication"
authors:
  - family-names: Kretski
    given-names: Dimitar
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Metal Science, Equipment and Technologies "Acad. A. Balevski",
      Center for Hydro- and Aerodynamics, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences
version: "2.1"
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kretski/residual-first-framework"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Residual-level cross-pulsar statistics applied to NANOGrav 15-yr and EPTA DR2
  timing residuals. A sky-scramble-calibrated Hellings–Downs test orthogonalised
  against monopole and dipole patterns gives p = 0.0135 (EPTA DR2full,
  pre-registered primary) and p = 0.0065 (DR2new, pre-registered secondary),
  recovering the known PTA signal. An omnibus cross-correlation statistic and
  temporal-shift nulls are shown to be miscalibrated on real PTA sampling.
keywords:
  - pulsar timing arrays
  - gravitational waves
  - Hellings-Downs correlation
  - pre-registration
  - calibration
  - NANOGrav
  - EPTA
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "The NANOGrav 15-Year Data Set (v2.1.0)"
    authors:
      - name: "The NANOGrav Collaboration"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.16051178"
  - type: dataset
    title: "EPTA DR2"
    authors:
      - name: "The EPTA Collaboration"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.8300645"
